# Wave T32 (Ashfall kit): ashfloor — Ashfall's own street kind.
# SWEPT ASH LANE: pale ash-cream gravel combed into long
# wind-drift streaks running the tile's length, sparse dark
# cinder flecks. A combed-drift surface: unlike Lilac's bronze
# lattice grid, Wildflower's loose petal scatter, Fairhaven's
# running-bond quay slabs, Copperton's square quarry flags,
# Mistford's timber plank floor. The painting's pale paths,
# drawn as the ash itself swept clean. (NO-SAME-KIT law;
# WAVE-T32-ASHFALL-PLAN.md.)
